changelog: |
  0.2.0 — markdown-oneline.yml floats actions/checkout and actions/setup-python
  to @v7. The fleet was ALREADY there: a mechanical action bump reached the 30
  deployed copies while this template stayed pinned at checkout@v4 /
  setup-python@v5, so any re-fanout would have silently downgraded 30 repos two
  major versions. archive/markdown-oneline-0.1.0.yml preserves the v4/v5 shape
  so `--upgrade` recognizes the two repos still on it (wtd, zpl-viewer) as
  machine-seeded and refreshes them, while hand-modified copies (it-journey
  adds generated-path excludes) are left alone.
  0.1.0 — initial kit: the Liquid-safe one-paragraph-per-line CI gate.
notes: |
  Deliberately NOT stamped with a `# kit:` comment the way agent-context is.
  Identity is established by byte-comparison against this template and the
  archive/ shapes, so bumping the kit costs the fleet nothing until the payload
  itself actually changes. Adding a stamp would mark all 30 current copies
  hand-modified and force a no-op PR into every repo.
